\section*{Generic Ramanujan for exceptional groups over function fields}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents the following claims relevant to this question, with manuscript numbers following paper order in Sources. In manuscript 1 (family 014; 2026-10-05), the asserted result is that globally generic cuspidal representations of split adjoint exceptional groups over function fields are tempered at ramified as well as unramified places, in every characteristic.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Manuscript 1.}
Let $F$ be a global function field and $G/F$ split connected adjoint absolutely simple of one of the exceptional types $G_2,F_4,E_6,E_7,E_8$. For every complex globally generic cuspidal automorphic representation $\pi=\bigotimes'_v\pi_v$ of $G(\mathbb A_F)$, the claimed conclusion is
\[
 \pi_v\text{ is tempered for every place }v.
\]
Ramified places are included. The statement imposes no characteristic, ramification-depth or local-representation-type restriction.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
For manuscript 1 (family 014; 2026-10-05), the companion unramified result supplies global purity. Local functional equations compare semisimple parameters independently of monodromy; regularity of the adjoint local factor then identifies the monodromy orbit needed to apply the local temperedness criterion.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The result supplies the conclusion in this problem with its displayed hypotheses and quantifiers. The broader statements and applications in the manuscript are kept separate from the particular question above. The supporting result is manuscript 1 (family 014; 2026-10-05).

